What is PySpark?

PySpark is the Python API for Apache Spark.

It is used to process large-scale data across multiple computers very fast.

In simple words:

Python + Spark = PySpark
You write code in Python
Spark handles big data processing in distributed systems
Why is PySpark used in Databricks?

Databricks is built on top of Apache Spark.

So PySpark is one of the main languages used inside Databricks for:

Data cleaning
Data transformation
ETL pipelines
Big data analytics
Machine learning preprocessing
Streaming data processing
Real-world Example

Suppose a company has:

500 million customer records
Sales data from many countries
Huge log files

Normal Python with pandas may become slow or crash because data is too large.

PySpark processes the data in parallel across clusters.
